title: PushNotifications
tags: [[TiddlyPWA Docs]]

TiddlyPWA supports **Web Push Notifications** and a three-tier extension system so you can build background watchers, due-date reminders, and interactive timers right inside your own TiddlyWiki.

!! Enabling Push on Your Device

# Open `$:/ControlPanel` → **TiddlyPWA** → **Push Notifications**.
# Click **Enable Push Notifications** and grant browser permission.
# Use **Send Test Notification** to verify delivery.

!! Choosing a Notification Tier

* **Tier 1 — Server Watchers (`module-type: pwa-watcher`)**: Sandboxed JavaScript ES modules synced to your server and executed on a cron schedule (for RSS/Atom feeds, JSON APIs, or web page scraping while your devices are offline).
* **Tier 2 — Declarative Due-Date Rules (`$:/tags/NotificationRule`)**: Zero-knowledge, client-encrypted notifications automatically scheduled from tiddler filters and date fields (e.g. `due`).
* **Tier 3 — Ad-Hoc Widget Messages (`tm-pwa-schedule-notification`)**: Zero-knowledge, client-encrypted one-off timers and reminders triggered from wikitext `<$button>` actions or JavaScript.

!! Tier 1: Server Watchers (`module-type: pwa-watcher`)

Create a tiddler with `type: application/javascript`, `module-type: pwa-watcher`, `watcher-id`, `schedule-cron`, and `allowed-hosts`:

```javascript
export async function evaluate(context, host) {
	const res = await host.fetch('https://news.ycombinator.com/rss');
	if (!res.ok || res.notModified) return [];
	const feed = await host.parseXml(res.body);
	const top = feed.items[0];
	if (!top || (await host.getState('lastGuid')) === top.guid) return [];
	await host.setState('lastGuid', top.guid);

	return [{
		notify: {
			title: 'Top HN Story',
			body: top.title,
			openUrl: top.link, // or navigateTo: 'HN: ' + top.title, or clickAction: 'none'
			actions: [{ action: 'open-wiki', title: 'Open in Wiki' }]
		},
		createTiddler: {
			title: 'HN: ' + top.title,
			text: top.link,
			tags: ['HN']
		},
		actionPatches: {
			'open-wiki': { navigateTo: 'HN: ' + top.title }
		}
	}];
}
```

!! Tier 2: Declarative Rules (`$:/tags/NotificationRule`)

Create a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/NotificationRule` with fields:
* `filter`: `[tag[Task]!tag[Done]has[due]]`
* `date-field`: `due` (supports TW timestamps, `YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYYMMDD`, or ISO strings)
* `default-time`: `09:00` (local time for date-only fields)
* `offset-minutes`: `-15`
* `title-template`: `Task Due: {{!!title}}`
* `body-template`: `Due at {{!!due}}`
* `navigate-to`, `url-field`, `open-url`, or `click-action`: control where clicking the notification goes

!! Tier 3: Widget Messages (`tm-pwa-schedule-notification`)

```tid
<$button>
  <$action-sendmessage
    $message="tm-pwa-schedule-notification"
    id="pomodoro-timer"
    delay-seconds="1500"
    title="Pomodoro Complete!"
    body="25 minutes elapsed."
    navigate-to="Pomodoro"
  />
  Start 25m Timer
</$button>
```
